comment.narrative:
Project net greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions sequestered calculated using the FAO Ex-ACT tool. Unit is tons of CO2 equivalent. The indicator corresponds to the PROGREEN indicator &#39;GHG emissions reduced in targeted landscapes (tons of CO2 equivalent)&quot; an a target for the PROGREEN source of fund is 1,900,000 tCO2eq.

As of December 31, 2024, the carbon footprint of the investments made was 198,608 TCO2 eq; i.e. a rate of achievement of the annual target of 8%. 
A revision of the final target will be considered due to the following: 
-	-the targets developed on the basis of the achievements of the PGDFEB;
-	the average surface area of the PGDFEB conservation areas was 1054.4 ha per municipality while it is about 553.4 ha for the first 30 municipalities;
-	large spaces, often heavily wooded, have been abandoned in favour of small spaces for reasons of encroachment.

Project net greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions sequestered calculated using the FAO Ex-ACT tool. Unit is tons of CO2 equivalent. The indicator corresponds to the PROGREEN indicator &#39;GHG emissions reduced in targeted landscapes (tons of CO2 equivalent)&quot; an a target for the PROGREEN source of fund is 1,900,000 tCO2eq.

To date,  the carbon footprint of the investments made is 471,140 TCO2 eq; i.e. a rate of achievement of the annual target of 9%. 
A revision of the final target will be considered due to the following: 
-	-the targets developed on the basis of the achievements of the PGDFEB;
-	the average surface area of the PGDFEB conservation areas was 1054.4 ha per municipality while it is about 553.4 ha for the first 30 municipalities;
-	large spaces, often heavily wooded, have been abandoned in favor of small spaces for reasons of encroachment.

The indicator measures, in hectares, the land area for which new and/or improved sustainable landscape management practices have been introduced. Land is the terrestrial biologically productive system comprising soil, vegetation, and the associated ecological and hydrological processes; Adoption refers to change of practice or change in the use of a technology promoted or introduced by the project; Sustainable landscape management (SLM) practices refers to a combination of at least two technologies and approaches to inrease land quality and restore degraded lands for example, agronomic, vegetative, structural, and management measures that, applied as a combination, increase the connectivity between protected areas, forest land, rangeland, and agriculture land.

This is an interim ISR and will be updated following a technical support mission mid-October.

